// g7250_main_fpga.repl — fused GPIOE + RF-FPGA port (M3 / D2).
//
// Replaces the stock gpioPortE with models/csharp/G7250Gpioe.cs
// `G7250GpioeFpga`, which is a full GPIO port that ALSO answers the FPGA's 8-bit
// bit-banged bus internally (HIS 80: D0-7=PE0-7, CMD=PE8, STB=PE9, DRDY=PE10).
// It handles the boot loopback bus-test (cmd 0x00), the version read (0x08), and
// pulses DRDY (PE10) so the sample routine reads changing 24-bit RX I/Q — the
// Main then logs "Check FPGA BUS... Check complete!" with no FPGA errors.
//
// Load procedure (the runner does this): compile the C# first
//   i @models/csharp/G7250Gpioe.cs
// then, after the base platform has registered gpioPortE,
//   sysbus Unregister sysbus.gpioPortE
//   machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/g7250_main_fpga.repl
// The [0-15] -> syscfg#4 line restores the EXTI routing (so DRDY/PE10 reaches
// EXTI15_10). Opt-in: the runtime-compiled port is slower, so m1_run uses it
// only with --fpga.
// Stock regression runs use a reduced DRDY rate (host speed); the model's
// default and product runs use the his/80 rate (48 kHz).
gpioPortE: Antmicro.Renode.Peripherals.GPIOPort.G7250GpioeFpga @ sysbus <0x58021000, +0x400>
    drdyRate: 4000
    [0-15] -> syscfg#4@[0-15]
